To create a program that can answer questions based on visual inputs, we will use a combination of the "Object_Detector_Tool" and "Text_Detector_Tool" tools. Here is the Python code to achieve this:

```python
import object_detector
import text_detector

def locate_interested_objects(image_path, labels=None, threshold=0.35, model_size='tiny', save_objects=False, saved_image_path="detected_objects"):
    detected_objects_result = object_detector.execute(image_path=image_path, labels=labels, threshold=threshold, model_size=model_size, save_object=save_objects, saved_image_path=saved_image_path)
    return detected_objects_result

def locate_letters_in_image(image_path):
    results = letter_detector.execute(image_path=image_path)
    return results

# Example usage
image_path = '/path/to/your_image.png'
object_result = locate_interested_objects(image_path, label='chair', save_objects=True)
print("Detected objects:", object_result)

letter_result = locate_letters_in_image("/path/to/audio/image.wav")
print("Detected letters:", letter_result)
```

Note: Replace `/path/to/your_image.png` and `/path/to/audio/image.wav` with the actual path of your image and audio file. Also, ensure the "object_detector" and "text_detector" tools are installed and functional.
